# Migration SQL is content-addressed: sqlx records a checksum of each
# file's bytes in `_sqlx_migrations`, and refuses to open a database
# whose recorded checksum disagrees with the file it compiled in
# (`VersionMismatch`, which fails Core::new and so fails startup).
#
# Windows checkouts default to core.autocrlf=true, so without this the
# same migration hashes differently depending on the host that built the
# binary: a Linux-built GMM and a Windows-built GMM would each refuse to
# open a database the other had migrated. Pinning LF makes the checksums
# a property of the repository rather than of whoever ran the build.
#
# tests/fixtures/migrations/*.db carry those checksums too; see
# docs/testing.md.
*.sql text eol=lf

# The corpus fixtures are SQLite files — never touch their bytes.
*.db binary
